ic process", "Metastatic visceral mass syndrome: weight loss and constitutional symptoms present but lack focal mass signs", "Diabetic ketoacidosis with CNS involvement: glucose normal, no metabolic derangements to support this"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B-symptoms (weight loss, night sweats, fever)", "Pancytopenia with blast lineage in peripheral blood", "Acute neurological decompensation (visual changes, ataxia) in systemic context"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5627061594729952, "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Blast morphology and constitutional symptoms are more typical of lymphoid neoplasms than other categories, with LR+ 6.0 indicating moderate support."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoid-specific features (T-cell receptor abnormalities, skin/endocrine manifestations) slightly reduces likelihood of lymphoid neoplasm."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.042, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation with peripheral blasts contradicts the indolent marrow-based course typical of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma C