ic process", "Metastatic visceral mass syndrome: weight loss and constitutional symptoms present but lack focal mass signs", "Diabetic ketoacidosis with CNS involvement: glucose normal, no metabolic derangements to support this"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B-symptoms (weight loss, night sweats, fever)", "Pancytopenia with blast lineage in peripheral blood", "Acute neurological decompensation (visual changes, ataxia) in systemic context"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5627061594729952, "posterior": 0.3998276443746328, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Blast morphology and constitutional symptoms are more typical of lymphoid neoplasms than other categories, with LR+ 6.0 indicating moderate support."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoid-specific features (T-cell receptor abnormalities, skin/endocrine manifestations) slightly reduces likelihood of lymphoid neoplasm."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.042, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation with peripheral blasts contradicts the indolent marrow-based course typical of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.037, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of lytic lesions and Bence Jones proteins (hallmarks of plasma cell disorders) weakly reduces likelihood of this category."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.012, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-Cell or T-Cell Variant)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.23840522560814154, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The high blast count and constitutional symptoms align with ALL, which typically presents with peripheral blasts and systemic features like weight loss and fev…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of T-cell receptor abnormalities weakly reduces the likelihood of ALL, but high peripheral blasts and constitutional symptoms maintain its plausibility."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1.1", "B2.1.2", "B2.1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": ["lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Lymphoblastic Lymphoma with Leukemic Phase", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.1614224187664913, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The neurological deficits suggest extramedullary disease, which is more characteristic of lymphoblastic lymphoma than ALL, but the absence of lymphoid-specific…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.2.1", "B2.2.2", "B2.2.3"], "closure_